--------------------------------------------------------------------------
ONE PART OF THIS REPOSITORY IS DIFFERENT: android/tts-bridge/
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything under `android/tts-bridge/` is licensed under the GNU General
Public License, version 3, NOT under the terms above. That directory contains
its own copy of the GPL-3.0 text, and each file in it carries its own licence
header.

That directory is a small, standalone speech engine bridge. It links espeak-ng
(by way of sherpa-onnx), which is GPL-3.0, so it is GPL-3.0 as well.

It is a SEPARATE PROGRAM from PhonoLeaf, not a component of it:

  * It runs in its own operating-system process (android:process=":tts").
  * PhonoLeaf reaches it only over Android's standard inter-process interface,
    sending text and primitive values and receiving audio written to a file
    path that PhonoLeaf chose. There is no shared memory, no callback into
    PhonoLeaf, and no custom type crossing the boundary.
  * It depends on nothing from PhonoLeaf. Its only dependencies are the
    Android framework, the Java standard library, and the speech engine. It
    could be reused unchanged by any other application.
  * No PhonoLeaf source file links, imports or references the speech engine.
    This is enforced automatically: `npm test` fails if any file outside that
    directory names it.

The two are combined only at packaging time, for practical distribution
through an app store.

See `android/tts-bridge/ENGINE_NOTICE.md` for the reasoning, and
`android/tts-bridge/LICENSE` for the GPL-3.0 text itself.

